  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: And if at the head of the recast protasis is one rendering of the single waw under rule 55's pair sentence, the two words being adjacent; the accepted added if is withdrawn.",
    "The and then later in the verse is a different case: the waw there holds its own and, no discourse-adverb morpheme stands beside it, and then is written as a second connective, so it remains added under rules 14 and 51.",
    "The margin's Hebrew to-day corroborates the fused reading of kayyom as first, and its textual note was read and set aside (rules 7 and 38). Variant unit v005 selected the base reading."
